      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:129:2",
      "text": [
        " الرَّجُلِ يُحْدِثُ فِي طَوَافِ الْفَرِيضَةِ وَ قَدْ طَافَ بَعْضَهُ قَالَ يَخْرُجُ فَيَتَوَضَّأُ فَإِنْ كَانَ جَازَ النِّصْفَ بَنَى عَلَى طَوَافِهِ وَ إِنْ كَانَ أَقَلَّ مِنَ النِّصْفِ أَعَادَ الطَّوَافَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from one of our companions, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from one of the two (5<sup>th</sup> or 6<sup>th</sup> Imam<sup>asws</sup>) regarding the man who excretes wind during the Obligatory <span class=\"iTxt\">Tawaaf</span>, and he had circumambulated part of it. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He should go out and perform ablution. So if he had completed the half, he would build upon his <span class=\"iTxt\">Tawaaf</span>; and if it was less than half, he would repeat the <span class=\"iTxt\">Tawaaf</span>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from certain persons of our people who has said the following: “One of the two Imam, (abu Ja’far or abu ‘Abd Allah), ‘Alayhim al-Salam, has said, Tf during obligatory Tawaf one’s wudu’ becomes invalid when he has performed a certain parts of Tawaf. he must take wudu’, and if he has performed more than half of Tawaf; he can continue from where he has left; but if what is performed is less than half he must perform Tawaf again.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
